From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:29:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] [CUDA] Support names for individual kernel launches

Upstream-base: tile-ai/tilelang@2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5
Upstream-commit: 78da73436947df60abff3e2c4ca7df5c3bf8d025

Rationale: Multi-launch @T.prim_func definitions previously suffixed every split device kernel from the parent function global_symbol without allowing per-launch descriptive names. Add name=... to T.Kernel(...) (propagated via launch_name attribute through SplitHostDevice) so individual kernel launches can carry distinct symbol names in traces and profiles.

Quality: Leaves unnamed T.Kernel(...) launches unchanged; complements vLLM patch 0118 for multi-launch prim_funcs.

Tests: testing/python/language/test_tilelang_language_kernel_name.py across two GPU boots on SM121.

Upstream-status: Backported from tile-ai/tilelang#3816 (commit 78da73436947df60abff3e2c4ca7df5c3bf8d025).
